 "answer": "In LlamaIndex, use **`Settings.chunk_size`** (from `llama_index.core`). It sets the chunk size for the default `SentenceSplitter` without replacing it:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\nSettings.chunk_size = 512\n```\n\nYou can also set **`Settings.chunk_overlap`** the same way. Both are read when the default node parser is created, so set them before you build your index or call the parser. If you've already accessed `Settings.node_parser` earlier in your code, the change may not take effect, so I'd recommend setting them first.",
